# Store-shot renders — regenerable from scripts/capture-store-shots.mjs and
# scripts/render-store-panel.mjs. The composition SOURCE (*.html) is tracked;
# the PNGs are not, because they are re-rendered on every iteration and would
# add a fresh multi-MB blob to history each time.
design/store-shots/raw/*
design/store-shots/*.png
# ...EXCEPT the device screenshots. Every other file under raw/ is produced by
# scripts/capture-store-shots.mjs and can be regenerated at will; these two come
# off a real iPhone because the screens they show carry a fractal-noise texture
# that Blink renders as per-pixel speckle and WebKit renders as tone. No script
# can reproduce them, so losing them would break the panels that use them.
!design/store-shots/raw/*-device.png

# Fuel-feature mockup renders — same deal. render.mjs rebuilds every PNG at the
# top of this folder from the *.html sources, and cutout.mjs rebuilds
# pump-node.png from raw/. Two exceptions are tracked because nothing can
# regenerate them: home-map.png (a cropped real-device Home screenshot — the
# map's noise texture does not survive a headless render) and everything under
# raw/, which is hand-made art. The rule below only matches the top level, so
# raw/ stays tracked by default.
design/fuel-mockup/*.png
!design/fuel-mockup/home-map.png
# Hero candidates: the ORIGINALS are tracked because prep-hero.mjs reads them and
# nothing can regenerate a photograph, but its output can always be rebuilt.
design/fuel-mockup/_hero-*-clean.jpeg
